        "Before choosing an income engine:\n- [ ] I understand the four income-engine categories.\n- [ ] I have assessed my skills and available resources.\n- [ ] I know how much capital I can safely risk.\n- [ ] I have considered how quickly I need cash.\n- [ ] I understand the main constraint of my chosen model.\n- [ ] I will test one model before splitting my attention.\n\nBefore selling a service:\n- [ ] I know the customer type I want to serve.\n- [ ] I understand a problem they actually experience.\n- [ ] My offer has a clear scope and deliverable.\n- [ ] I have a relevant sample or demonstration.\n- [ ] My price reflects the scope and my current ability.\n- [ ] I have not promised an outcome I cannot substantiate.\n- [ ] I can deliver the work within the agreed timeline.\n\nBefore accepting a client:\n- [ ] The problem and expected outcome are clear.\n- [ ] The scope and exclusions are documented.\n- [ ] Payment terms are agreed.\n- [ ] Client responsibilities are clear.\n- [ ] Deadlines and milestones are realistic.\n- [ ] Communication and revision expectations are agreed.\n- [ ] The project is recorded in my tracking system.\n\nBefore scaling:\n- [ ] I can deliver the current workload reliably.\n- [ ] I know which customers and offers are most profitable.\n- [ ] I have a repeatable workflow.\n- [ ] I have a consistent source of qualified opportunities.\n- [ ] I track cash flow and upcoming obligations.\n- [ ] I am improving the process rather than simply adding hours.\n\nBefore investing:\n- [ ] Essential expenses and near-term obligations are covered.\n- [ ] I have an appropriate cash reserve.\n- [ ] I understand the investment.\n- [ ] I understand the risks and costs.\n- [ ] I have considered taxes and local regulations.\n- [ ] The time horizon matches the asset's risk.\n- [ ] I am not investing money I cannot afford to lose in speculative assets.\n- [ ] My decision is based on a plan rather than hype."
